---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="about" description={`About ${SITE.title}`}>
  <div class="about-head">
    <img src="/avatar.png" alt={`${SITE.title} avatar`} width="92" height="92" />
    <div>
      <h1>{SITE.title}</h1>
      <span class="handle">{SITE.handle}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Independent security researcher and bug bounty hunter. I break web apps,
      cloud infrastructure, and APIs for a living — then write up what actually
      worked. Focus areas: authentication bypass, SSRF, IDOR &amp; broken access
      control, and business-logic flaws that scanners never find.
    </p>
    <p>
      This blog is where the interesting chains land — the ones where a couple of
      "low-severity" quirks stack into something a program actually pays for.
      Everything here is from authorized testing on programs where I had explicit
      permission to hunt.
    </p>

    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Full write-ups with reproducible steps and real impact.</li>
      <li>Short exploit notes and reusable primitives.</li>
      <li>Methodology — how the bug was found, not just what it was.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Rules of engagement</h2>
    <p>
      No proof of concept, no post. I don't publish anything theoretical, and I
      don't name unfixed targets. If it's here, it was reported, triaged, and
      resolved first.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Reach me through the links in the header. For anything sensitive, use an
      encrypted channel and I'll share a key.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
